{"id":"tha-t1-0001","lang":"tha","tier":1,"slot":"count.eight","domain":2,"text_native":"๘ แปด","text_romanized":"paet","text_english":"Eight.","source_caption":"8","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Continuing the count.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Thai phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Thai_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tha-t1-0002","lang":"tha","tier":1,"slot":"count.five","domain":2,"text_native":"๕ ห้า","text_romanized":"haa","text_english":"Five.","source_caption":"5","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Five is where most of these languages change to a different counting pattern, and knowing that in advance is the point of learning them in order.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Thai phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Thai_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tha-t1-0003","lang":"tha","tier":1,"slot":"count.four","domain":2,"text_native":"๔ สี่","text_romanized":"sii","text_english":"Four.","source_caption":"4","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Continuing the count.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Thai phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Thai_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tha-t1-0004","lang":"tha","tier":1,"slot":"count.nine","domain":2,"text_native":"๙ เก้า","text_romanized":"kao","text_english":"Nine.","source_caption":"9","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Continuing the count.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Thai phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Thai_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tha-t1-0005","lang":"tha","tier":1,"slot":"count.one","domain":2,"text_native":"๑ หนึ่ง on its own, (et) เอ็ด in compounds","text_romanized":"nueng","text_english":"One.","source_caption":"1","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Counting from one upward in order, because a traveller counts by reciting rather than by arithmetic.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Thai phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Thai_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tha-t1-0006","lang":"tha","tier":1,"slot":"count.seven","domain":2,"text_native":"๗ เจ็ด","text_romanized":"jet","text_english":"Seven.","source_caption":"7","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Continuing the count.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Thai phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Thai_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tha-t1-0007","lang":"tha","tier":1,"slot":"count.six","domain":2,"text_native":"๖ หก","text_romanized":"hok","text_english":"Six.","source_caption":"6","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Continuing the count.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Thai phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Thai_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tha-t1-0008","lang":"tha","tier":1,"slot":"count.ten","domain":2,"text_native":"๑๐ สิบ","text_romanized":"sip","text_english":"Ten.","source_caption":"10","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The first number past the counting pattern in most of these languages.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Thai phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Thai_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tha-t1-0009","lang":"tha","tier":1,"slot":"count.three","domain":2,"text_native":"๓ สาม","text_romanized":"saam","text_english":"Three.","source_caption":"3","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Continuing the count.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Thai phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Thai_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tha-t1-0010","lang":"tha","tier":1,"slot":"count.two","domain":2,"text_native":"๒ สอง","text_romanized":"song","text_english":"Two.","source_caption":"2","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Continuing the count.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Thai phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Thai_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tha-t1-0011","lang":"tha","tier":1,"slot":"count.zero","domain":2,"text_native":"๐ ศูนย์","text_romanized":"suun","text_english":"None, zero.","source_caption":"0","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Zero is the answer that gets misheard most often, because the word for nothing and the word for a small quantity are often unrelated.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Thai phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Thai_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tha-t1-0012","lang":"tha","tier":1,"slot":"price.bill","domain":3,"text_native":"เก็บเงินด้วย","text_romanized":"kèb ngern dûai","text_english":"The bill, please.","source_caption":"The check, please.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Where the word for bill and the word for receipt are the same word and neither is 'account'.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Thai phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Thai_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tha-t1-0013","lang":"tha","tier":1,"slot":"price.card-ok","domain":3,"text_native":"คุณรับบัตรเครดิตไหม","text_romanized":"kun ráp bàt kre-dìt măi","text_english":"Is card payment accepted?","source_caption":"Do you accept credit cards?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The alternative to carrying cash, and the question that decides whether you are standing in a queue that moves.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Thai phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Thai_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tha-t1-0014","lang":"tha","tier":1,"slot":"price.how-much","domain":3,"text_native":"นี่เท่าไหร่?","text_romanized":"nîi thâo rài?","text_english":"How much is this?","source_caption":"How much is this?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The most useful question in the tier, and the one people are most afraid to ask. It is not rude anywhere.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Thai phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Thai_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tha-t1-0015","lang":"tha","tier":1,"slot":"price.too-cheap","domain":3,"text_native":"ถูก","text_romanized":"thùuk","text_english":"It is cheaper in my country.","source_caption":"cheap","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Read as an accusation almost everywhere. Included because knowing that it is an accusation is worth more than being able to say it politely.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Thai phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Thai_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tha-t1-0016","lang":"tha","tier":1,"slot":"price.too-expensive","domain":3,"text_native":"แพงไป","text_romanized":"phaeng pai","text_english":"That is too expensive.","source_caption":"That's too expensive.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Used with the hand gesture that accompanies it. The gesture carries the meaning and the word confirms it.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Thai phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Thai_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tha-t1-0017","lang":"tha","tier":1,"slot":"money.atm","domain":3,"text_native":"เอทีเอ็มอยู่ที่ไหน","text_romanized":"e thii em yùu thîi năi","text_english":"Where is an ATM?","source_caption":"Where is an automatic teller machine (ATM)?","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"Recognising rather than producing it: you will be shown the sign rather than expected to ask.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Thai phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Thai_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tha-t1-0018","lang":"tha","tier":1,"slot":"money.change","domain":3,"text_native":"คุณจะแลกเปลี่ยนสกุลเงินกับผม/ดิฉันไหม","text_romanized":"kun jà laek plìen sà-kun ngern kùb phŏm/dì-chăn mǎi","text_english":"Please change this into local money.","source_caption":"Can you change money for me?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The word 'change' means both coins and alteration in several of these languages, and the wrong one is confusing.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Thai phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Thai_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tha-t1-0019","lang":"tha","tier":1,"slot":"money.exchange-rate","domain":3,"text_native":"อัตราแลกเปลี่ยนเท่าไร","text_romanized":"àt-traa lâek plìen tâo rài","text_english":"What is the exchange rate?","source_caption":"What is the exchange rate?","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"Often answered by pointing at a board rather than spoken.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Thai phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Thai_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tha-t1-0020","lang":"tha","tier":1,"slot":"toilet.where","domain":12,"text_native":"ห้องน้ำ","text_romanized":"hông náam","text_english":"Where is the toilet?","source_caption":"Toilet","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The most urgent question in this tier and the one every phrasebook leads with. In several languages the word is the only one a traveller needs for years.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Thai phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Thai_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tha-t1-0021","lang":"tha","tier":1,"slot":"food.delicious","domain":4,"text_native":"อร่อย","text_romanized":"a-ròi","text_english":"It is delicious.","source_caption":"Delicious.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The cheapest goodwill available, and in some of these languages the only correct way to receive a dish rather than simply eat it.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Thai phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Thai_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tha-t1-0022","lang":"tha","tier":1,"slot":"food.menu","domain":4,"text_native":"ขอดูเมนูครับ/ค่ะ","text_romanized":"khǒ duu menuu khráp/khà","text_english":"The menu, please.","source_caption":"Can I look at the menu, please?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"One question covers a whole meal. Most phrasebooks waste slots on individual dishes instead.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Thai phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Thai_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tha-t1-0023","lang":"tha","tier":1,"slot":"food.no-meat","domain":4,"text_native":"ผม/ดิฉัน ไม่กินหมู","text_romanized":"phŏm/dì-chăn mâi kin mǔu","text_english":"I do not eat meat.","source_caption":"I don't eat pork.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Saying it once at the start of the trip saves a refusal at the table, where it is awkward for both sides.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Thai phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Thai_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tha-t1-0024","lang":"tha","tier":1,"slot":"food.water","domain":4,"text_native":"น้ำเปล่า","text_romanized":"náam plào","text_english":"Water, please.","source_caption":"water","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Refusing the water in a restaurant is a small discourtesy in several of these countries. This is how to ask for some instead.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Thai phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Thai_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tha-t1-0025","lang":"tha","tier":1,"slot":"food.what-is-this","domain":4,"text_native":"นี่อะไร","text_romanized":"nii a-rai","text_english":"What is this?","source_caption":"What is this?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"For a dish whose name you cannot read and have to be told.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Thai phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Thai_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tha-t1-0026","lang":"tha","tier":1,"slot":"way.straight","domain":7,"text_native":"ตรงไป","text_romanized":"trong pai","text_english":"Go straight ahead.","source_caption":"straight ahead","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"Recognised rather than produced.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Thai phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Thai_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tha-t1-0027","lang":"tha","tier":1,"slot":"way.turn-left","domain":7,"text_native":"เลี้ยวซ้าย","text_romanized":"liaao saai","text_english":"Turn left.","source_caption":"Turn left.","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"Recognised rather than produced: you are the one being given directions far more often than giving them.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Thai phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Thai_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tha-t1-0028","lang":"tha","tier":1,"slot":"way.turn-right","domain":7,"text_native":"เลี้ยวขวา","text_romanized":"liaao khwaa","text_english":"Turn right.","source_caption":"Turn right.","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"Recognised rather than produced.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Thai phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Thai_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tha-t1-0029","lang":"tha","tier":1,"slot":"stay.checkout","domain":5,"text_native":"ผมต้องการเช็คเอ้าท์.","text_romanized":"pǒm/dì-chăn tông kaan check out","text_english":"I would like to check out, please.","source_caption":"I want to check out.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Said the morning before leaving, so the bill is not waiting at the desk while luggage is being gathered.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Thai phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Thai_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tha-t1-0030","lang":"tha","tier":1,"slot":"move.destination","domain":6,"text_native":"พาผม/ดิฉันไปที่นั่นหน่อยครับ/ค่ะ","text_romanized":"phaa phŏm/dì-chăn pai tîi nân nòi khrap/khâ","text_english":"Please take me there.","source_caption":"Take me there, please.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Shown with a map or a written address while saying it. 'There' is the word the pages use; 'this address' is in none of them, and a slot phrased from imagination rather than from a caption is a slot that can never be filled.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Thai phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Thai_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tha-t1-0031","lang":"tha","tier":1,"slot":"health.doctor","domain":9,"text_native":"ผม/ฉัน ต้องการหมอ","text_romanized":"phom/chan tongkaan mö","text_english":"I need a doctor.","source_caption":"I need a doctor.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Short enough to say to anyone, which is the point — a phrase you cannot finish is a phrase that arrives too late.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Thai phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Thai_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tha-t1-0032","lang":"tha","tier":1,"slot":"health.hurt","domain":9,"text_native":"ผม/ฉัน บาดเจ็บ","text_romanized":"phom/chan baat jep","text_english":"I have been injured.","source_caption":"I've been injured.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Declares the situation before being asked. Several of these languages change tense or register on the word for injury, and the flat version sounds like a complaint.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Thai phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Thai_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tha-t1-0033","lang":"tha","tier":1,"slot":"help.dont-touch","domain":10,"text_native":"อย่าจับ ผม/ฉัน!","text_romanized":"yàa jàp phŏm (men)/chan (for women","text_english":"Do not touch me.","source_caption":"Don't touch me!","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Out loud and to a person, not shouted generally. Several of these languages treat it as an accusation, so it is a sentence to use deliberately.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Thai phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Thai_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tha-t1-0034","lang":"tha","tier":1,"slot":"help.emergency","domain":10,"text_native":"เรื่องฉุกเฉิน","text_romanized":"rueang chuk chern","text_english":"It is an emergency.","source_caption":"It's an emergency.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Changes how the next thirty seconds go. Two words, and in several of these languages it reaches a different set of responses than a request would.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Thai phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Thai_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tha-t1-0035","lang":"tha","tier":1,"slot":"help.leave-me-alone","domain":10,"text_native":"อย่ายุ่งกับ ผม/ฉัน","text_romanized":"yàa yung kap phŏm (for men)/chan (for women","text_english":"Please leave me alone.","source_caption":"Leave me alone.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Said firmly and quietly. Raising the volume is what turns it from a boundary into an incident in several of these cultures.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Thai phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Thai_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tha-t1-0036","lang":"tha","tier":1,"slot":"help.lost","domain":10,"text_native":"ผม/ฉัน หลงทาง","text_romanized":"phom/chan long thaang","text_english":"I am lost.","source_caption":"I'm lost.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Asking a passer-by for help is a separate skill from reading a sign, and it uses different vocabulary in every one of these languages.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Thai phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Thai_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tha-t1-0037","lang":"tha","tier":1,"slot":"help.phone","domain":10,"text_native":"ผม/ฉัน ขอใช้โทรศัพท์ได้ไหม","text_romanized":"phom/chan kho chai thorasap dai mai","text_english":"Can I use your phone?","source_caption":"Can I use your phone?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The most common thing a traveller needs that a phone provides, and asking a stranger for it is usually granted.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Thai phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Thai_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tha-t1-0038","lang":"tha","tier":1,"slot":"help.police","domain":10,"text_native":"ผม/ฉัน จะแจ้งตำรวจ","text_romanized":"phom/chan ja jaang taamruat","text_english":"Please call the police.","source_caption":"I'll call the police.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Usually needs a phone, and in most places a local number rather than an international one.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Thai phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Thai_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"tha-t1-0039","lang":"tha","tier":1,"slot":"help.thief","domain":10,"text_native":"หยุด! โจร/ขโมย!","text_romanized":"yut jon/khamoy","text_english":"Stop, thief!","source_caption":"Stop! Thief!","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Loud, and aimed at a crowd rather than at one person. Included because the vocabulary exists and because it is the sentence that makes people nearby move.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Thai phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Thai_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
